IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-builders`

-- ccc6-sexual-offences.l4 -- ss 151, 152, 153, 155 and 156: sexual interference, invitation, sexual exploitation, incest, historical offences.
-- (s 153.1 is in ccc6-s153-1.l4, s 160 in ccc6-bestiality.l4; the repealed ss 154, 157 to 159 are in ccc6-repealed.l4.)
-- An offence function answers JUST TRUE when every element is met on the facts given and NOTHING otherwise: the text says "every person who ... is guilty", it does not say that
-- a person who does less is innocent of it, and an element is a limit in the offence's own wording (fork F1). A punishment function answers a core `Punishment` for one limb.

§ `s 151 Sexual interference`

-- src:3025 | Sexual interference
-- src:3026 | 151 Every person who, for a sexual purpose, touches, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, any part of the body of a person under the age of 16 years
-- src:3027 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:3028 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of 90 days.
@ref Criminal Code s 151 (src:3025-3028)
GIVEN `the person touched, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, a part of the body of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the touching was for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age in years of the person touched` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 151 the conduct is sexual interference` MEANS
    IF    `the person touched, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, a part of the body of another person`
      AND `the touching was for a sexual purpose`
      AND `the age in years of the person touched` LESS THAN 16
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who, for a sexual purpose, touches, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, any part of the body of a person under the age of 16 years"

@ref Criminal Code s 151(a) (src:3027)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 151(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 151(b) (src:3028)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 151(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ninety days`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 151 (src:3026-3028)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 151 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§ `s 152 Invitation to sexual touching or exposure`

-- src:3029 | Invitation to sexual touching or exposure
-- src:3030 | 152 (1) Every person commits an offence who, for a sexual purpose, invites, counsels or incites a person under the age of 16 years to
-- src:3031 | (a) touch, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, their own body, the body of the person who so invites, counsels or incites or the body of any other person; or
-- src:3032 | (b) expose their own sexual organs.
@ref Criminal Code s 152(1) (src:3029-3032)
DECLARE `s 152(1) what the person is invited, counselled or incited to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 152(1)(a) touch, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, their own body, the body of the person who so invites, counsels or incites or the body of any other person`
    `s 152(1)(b) expose their own sexual organs`
    `s 152(1) something else`

GIVEN `the person invited, counselled or incited another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was done for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age in years of the person invited, counselled or incited` IS A NUMBER
      `what the other person was invited, counselled or incited to do` IS A `s 152(1) what the person is invited, counselled or incited to do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(1) the conduct is the offence of invitation to sexual touching or exposure` MEANS
    IF    `the person invited, counselled or incited another person`
      AND `it was done for a sexual purpose`
      AND `the age in years of the person invited, counselled or incited` LESS THAN 16
      AND (   `what the other person was invited, counselled or incited to do` EQUALS `s 152(1)(a) touch, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, their own body, the body of the person who so invites, counsels or incites or the body of any other person`
           OR `what the other person was invited, counselled or incited to do` EQUALS `s 152(1)(b) expose their own sexual organs`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who, for a sexual purpose, invites, counsels or incites a person under the age of 16 years to (a) touch, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, their own body, the body of the person who so invites, counsels or incites or the body of any other person; or (b) expose their own sexual organs"

-- src:3033 | Punishment
-- src:3034 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:3035 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:3036 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of 90 days.
@ref Criminal Code s 152(2) (src:3033-3036)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 152(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 152(2)(b) (src:3036)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 152(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ninety days`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 152(2) (src:3033-3036)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 152 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§ `s 153 Sexual exploitation`

-- src:3052 | Definition of young person
-- src:3053 | (2) In this section, young person means a person 16 years of age or more but under the age of eighteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 153(2) (src:3052-3053)
GIVEN `the age of the person in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153(2) young person` MEANS
    IF `the age of the person in years` AT LEAST 16 AND `the age of the person in years` LESS THAN 18
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "young person means a person 16 years of age or more but under the age of eighteen years"

DECLARE `s 153(1) what the person did to the young person` IS ONE OF
    `s 153(1)(a) for a sexual purpose, touched, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, any part of the body of the young person`
    `s 153(1)(b) for a sexual purpose, invited, counselled or incited a young person to touch, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, their own body, the body of the person who so invites, counsels or incites or the body of any other person`
    `s 153(1)(c) for a sexual purpose, invited, counselled or incited the young person to expose their own sexual organs`
    `s 153(1) something else`

-- src:3037 | Sexual exploitation
-- src:3038 | 153 (1) Every person commits an offence who is in a position of trust or authority towards a young person, who is a person with whom the young person is in a relationship of dependency or who is in a relationship with a young person that is exploitative of the young person, and who
-- src:3039 | (a) for a sexual purpose, touches, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, any part of the body of the young person;
-- src:3040 | (b) for a sexual purpose, invites, counsels or incites a young person to touch, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object, their own body, the body of the person who so invites, counsels or incites or the body of any other person; or
-- src:3041 | (c) for a sexual purpose, invites, counsels or incites the young person to expose their own sexual organs.
@ref Criminal Code s 153(1) (src:3037-3041)
GIVEN `the person is in a position of trust or authority towards the young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person with whom the young person is in a relationship of dependency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in a relationship with the young person that is exploitative of the young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of the young person in years` IS A NUMBER
      `what the person did` IS A `s 153(1) what the person did to the young person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153(1) the conduct is the offence of sexual exploitation` MEANS
    IF    (   `the person is in a position of trust or authority towards the young person`
           OR `the person is a person with whom the young person is in a relationship of dependency`
           OR `the person is in a relationship with the young person that is exploitative of the young person`)
      AND `s 153(2) young person` `the age of the young person in years` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND NOT (`what the person did` EQUALS `s 153(1) something else`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who is in a position of trust or authority towards a young person, who is a person with whom the young person is in a relationship of dependency or who is in a relationship with a young person that is exploitative of the young person, and who (a) for a sexual purpose, touches"

-- src:3042 | Punishment
-- src:3043 | (1.1) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:3044 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:3045 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of 90 days.
@ref Criminal Code s 153(1.1) (src:3042-3045)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 153(1.1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 153(1.1)(b) (src:3045)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 153(1.1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ninety days`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 153(1.1) (src:3042-3045)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 153 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (1.2) "A judge may infer ...": a power of the judge, named "may" (the ruling of 2026-11-12). It has no "if": the inference must be drawn "from the nature and circumstances of the relationship, including" (a) to (d).
-- "including" leaves the list open, so any circumstance of the relationship is a basis; a matter that is not part of the relationship's nature and circumstances is outside the grant: NOTHING.
-- src:3046 | Inference of sexual exploitation
-- src:3047 | (1.2) A judge may infer that a person is in a relationship with a young person that is exploitative of the young person from the nature and circumstances of the relationship, including
-- src:3048 | (a) the age of the young person;
-- src:3049 | (b) the age difference between the person and the young person;
-- src:3050 | (c) the evolution of the relationship; and
-- src:3051 | (d) the degree of control or influence by the person over the young person.
@ref Criminal Code s 153(1.2) (src:3046-3051)
DECLARE `s 153(1.2) what the inference is drawn from` IS ONE OF
    `s 153(1.2)(a) the age of the young person`
    `s 153(1.2)(b) the age difference between the person and the young person`
    `s 153(1.2)(c) the evolution of the relationship`
    `s 153(1.2)(d) the degree of control or influence by the person over the young person`
    `s 153(1.2) another circumstance of the relationship`
    `s 153(1.2) a matter that is not part of the nature and circumstances of the relationship`

GIVEN `what the inference is drawn from` IS A `s 153(1.2) what the inference is drawn from`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153(1.2) a judge may infer from it that the relationship is exploitative of the young person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what the inference is drawn from`
    WHEN `s 153(1.2)(a) the age of the young person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 153(1.2)(b) the age difference between the person and the young person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 153(1.2)(c) the evolution of the relationship` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 153(1.2)(d) the degree of control or influence by the person over the young person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 153(1.2) another circumstance of the relationship` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 153(1.2) a matter that is not part of the nature and circumstances of the relationship` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "from the nature and circumstances of the relationship, including"

§ `s 155 Incest`

-- (4) "brother and sister, respectively, include half-brother and half-sister": for the purposes of s 155 only ("In this section").
DECLARE `s 155 the other person is, by blood relationship, the person's` IS ONE OF
    `s 155 parent`
    `s 155 child`
    `s 155 brother`
    `s 155 sister`
    `s 155 half-brother`
    `s 155 half-sister`
    `s 155 grandparent`
    `s 155 grandchild`
    `s 155 another relative, or no blood relationship`

-- src:3095 | Definition of brother and sister
-- src:3096 | (4) In this section, brother and sister, respectively, include half-brother and half-sister.
@ref Criminal Code s 155(4) (src:3095-3096)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 155 the other person is, by blood relationship, the person's`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(4) brother and sister include half-brother and half-sister` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `s 155 brother` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 155 sister` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 155 half-brother` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 155 half-sister` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "brother and sister, respectively, include half-brother and half-sister"

-- src:3089 | Incest
-- src:3090 | 155 (1) Every one commits incest who, knowing that another person is by blood relationship his or her parent, child, brother, sister, grandparent or grandchild, as the case may be, has sexual intercourse with that person.
@ref Criminal Code s 155(1) (src:3089-3090)
GIVEN `the person knew of the blood relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      relationship IS A `s 155 the other person is, by blood relationship, the person's`
      `the person had sexual intercourse with the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(1) the conduct is incest` MEANS
    IF    `the person knew of the blood relationship`
      AND `the person had sexual intercourse with the other person`
      AND (   relationship EQUALS `s 155 parent`
           OR relationship EQUALS `s 155 child`
           OR relationship EQUALS `s 155 grandparent`
           OR relationship EQUALS `s 155 grandchild`
           OR `s 155(4) brother and sister include half-brother and half-sister` relationship EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one commits incest who, knowing that another person is by blood relationship his or her parent, child, brother, sister, grandparent or grandchild, as the case may be, has sexual intercourse with that person"

-- (2) one limb only: indictable. The minimum of five years applies "if the other person is under the age of 16 years".
-- src:3091 | Punishment
-- src:3092 | (2) Everyone who commits incest is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and, if the other person is under the age of 16 years, to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of five years.
@ref Criminal Code s 155(2) (src:3091-3092)
GIVEN `the age in years of the other person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 155(2) the punishment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`
                , `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`
                , IF `the age in years of the other person` LESS THAN 16 THEN `imprisonment for a term of` `five years` ELSE `no imprisonment is stated`
                , `no fine is stated`
                , `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 155(2) (src:3092)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 155 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- (3) "No accused shall be determined by a court to be guilty ... if the accused was under restraint, duress or fear of the person ... at the time": a defence.
-- JUST TRUE when one of the three held; otherwise JUST FALSE, "this section gives no defence on these facts" (the delegated-defence ruling (b) of 2026-11-05), never "no defence at all".
-- src:3093 | Defence
-- src:3094 | (3) No accused shall be determined by a court to be guilty of an offence under this section if the accused was under restraint, duress or fear of the person with whom the accused had the sexual intercourse at the time the sexual intercourse occurred.
@ref Criminal Code s 155(3) (src:3093-3094)
GIVEN `the accused was under restraint of the person with whom the accused had the sexual intercourse at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was under duress of that person at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was under fear of that person at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 155(3) section 155 gives the accused a defence` MEANS
    IF    `the accused was under restraint of the person with whom the accused had the sexual intercourse at the time`
       OR `the accused was under duress of that person at the time`
       OR `the accused was under fear of that person at the time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the accused was under restraint, duress or fear of the person with whom the accused had the sexual intercourse at the time the sexual intercourse occurred"

§ `s 156 Historical offences`

-- "No person shall be convicted of any sexual offence under this Act as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983 unless the conduct alleged would be an offence under this Act if it occurred on the day on which the charge was laid."
-- src:3097 | Historical offences
-- src:3098 | 156 No person shall be convicted of any sexual offence under this Act as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983 unless the conduct alleged would be an offence under this Act if it occurred on the day on which the charge was laid.
@ref Criminal Code s 156 (src:3097-3098)
GIVEN `the offence charged is a sexual offence under this Act as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct alleged would be an offence under this Act if it occurred on the day on which the charge was laid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156 no person shall be convicted: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence charged is a sexual offence under this Act as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person shall be convicted of any sexual offence under this Act as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983"
        IF `the conduct alleged would be an offence under this Act if it occurred on the day on which the charge was laid`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the conduct alleged would be an offence under this Act if it occurred on the day on which the charge was laid"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
